{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ML-07 — Baseline Action Score and Top-10 Review\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook builds a transparent, rule-based review queue for content refresh work. The score is a decision-support baseline, not a causal model or a forecast.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. My rule and its reason codes\n",
    "\n",
    "A page should move up the review queue when it has **visible demand** but also shows a practical opportunity: it is old, sits in a weak search position, has a low click-through rate for its visibility, or is unusually short.\n",
    "\n",
    "The two signal checks carried forward from the audit are:\n",
    "1. **Visibility × freshness:** stale pages with meaningful impressions are plausible refresh candidates because a team can improve something that already receives search exposure.\n",
    "2. **Visibility × search opportunity:** pages with impressions but weak position or low CTR deserve review because they have observable search demand without equally strong click performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "The score uses only snapshot features available before review. It deliberately does **not** use `trend_direction`, `trend_pct`, or `is_declining_label`; those are reserved for evaluation because the label is derived from trend.\n",
    "\n",
    "Reason codes: `stale_visible_page`, `position_opportunity`, `low_ctr_visible_page`, `thin_visible_page`, and `general_review`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep the notebook runnable both from the repository and from Colab.\n",
    "candidate_paths = [\n",
    "    Path('data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv'),\n",
    "    Path('../../data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv'),\n",
    "    Path('/content/my_ML_Intership_at_FLYRANK-AI/data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv'),\n",
    "]\n",
    "data_path = next((p for p in candidate_paths if p.exists()), None)\n",
    "if data_path is None:\n",
    "    data_path = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/iamuhd/my_ML_Intership_at_FLYRANK-AI/main/data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv'\n",
    "\n",
    "raw = pd.read_csv(data_path)\n",
    "required = ['content_id', 'client_id', 'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr',\n",
    "            'days_since_last_update', 'word_count', 'engagement_rate',\n",
    "            'trend_direction']\n",
    "missing = sorted(set(required) - set(raw.columns))\n",
    "if missing:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f'Missing required columns: {missing}')\n",
    "\n",
    "df = raw[(raw['impressions_90d'] > 0) & (raw['content_age_days'] >= 90)].copy()\n",
    "df = df.drop_duplicates('content_id').reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "for column in ['impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr', 'days_since_last_update',\n",
    "               'word_count', 'engagement_rate', 'scroll_rate', 'sessions_90d']:\n",
    "    if column in df:\n",
    "        df[column] = pd.to_numeric(df[column], errors='coerce').replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan).fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "def percentile_rank(values):\n",
    "    return pd.Series(values).rank(method='average', pct=True).fillna(0).to_numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "def minmax(values):\n",
    "    values = pd.Series(values).astype(float).fillna(0)\n",
    "    lo, hi = values.min(), values.max()\n",
    "    if hi == lo:\n",
    "        return pd.Series(0.0, index=values.index)\n",
    "    return (values - lo) / (hi - lo)\n",
    "\n",
    "def make_reason_codes(row):\n",
    "    reasons = []\n",
    "    visible = row['impressions_90d'] >= 500\n",
    "    if row['days_since_last_update'] >= 180 and visible:\n",
    "        reasons.append('stale_visible_page')\n",
    "    if visible and 0 < row['avg_position'] <= 20:\n",
    "        reasons.append('position_opportunity')\n",
    "    if visible and 0 < row['avg_position'] <= 20 and row['ctr'] < 0.5:\n",
    "        reasons.append('low_ctr_visible_page')\n",
    "    if 0 < row['word_count'] < 1200 and row['impressions_90d'] >= 250:\n",
    "        reasons.append('thin_visible_page')\n",
    "    return '|'.join(reasons) if reasons else 'general_review'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Rows screened: {len(df):,}')\n",
    "print(f'Observed declining-label base rate: {df["trend_direction"].eq("down").mean():.3f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build the ranked queue (writes the CSV)\n",
    "\n",
    "The score is intentionally readable: visibility supplies opportunity, while freshness, position, CTR, and content depth add review priority. Percentile ranks reduce the effect of the heavy-tailed impression distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "visibility = pd.Series(percentile_rank(np.log1p(df['impressions_90d'])), index=df.index)\n",
    "freshness_risk = pd.Series(percentile_rank(df['days_since_last_update']), index=df.index)\n",
    "position_quality = (1 - minmax(df['avg_position'].clip(lower=1, upper=50)))\n",
    "position_quality = position_quality * (df['avg_position'] > 0).astype(int)\n",
    "position_opportunity = position_quality * visibility\n",
    "low_ctr_opportunity = (1 - minmax(df['ctr'].clip(lower=0, upper=df['ctr'].quantile(0.99)))) * visibility\n",
    "depth_gap = (1 - pd.Series(percentile_rank(df['word_count']), index=df.index)) * visibility\n",
    "\n",
    "df['visibility_score'] = visibility\n",
    "df['freshness_risk_score'] = freshness_risk\n",
    "df['position_opportunity_score'] = position_opportunity\n",
    "df['low_ctr_opportunity_score'] = low_ctr_opportunity\n",
    "df['depth_gap_score'] = depth_gap\n",
    "df['baseline_action_score'] = (\n",
    "    0.35 * visibility\n",
    "    + 0.25 * freshness_risk\n",
    "    + 0.20 * position_opportunity\n",
    "    + 0.15 * low_ctr_opportunity\n",
    "    + 0.05 * depth_gap\n",
    ").clip(0, 1)\n",
    "df['reason_codes'] = df.apply(make_reason_codes, axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "def suggested_action(code):\n",
    "    code = set(str(code).split('|'))\n",
    "    if 'thin_visible_page' in code:\n",
    "        return 'expand_and_refresh'\n",
    "    if 'low_ctr_visible_page' in code or 'position_opportunity' in code:\n",
    "        return 'refresh_and_review_ctr'\n",
    "    if 'stale_visible_page' in code:\n",
    "        return 'refresh'\n",
    "    return 'monitor'\n",
    "\n",
    "df['suggested_action'] = df['reason_codes'].map(suggested_action)\n",
    "df = df.sort_values(['baseline_action_score', 'impressions_90d'], ascending=[False, False]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "df['baseline_rank'] = np.arange(1, len(df) + 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "output_columns = [\n",
    "    'content_id', 'client_id', 'baseline_rank', 'baseline_action_score',\n",
    "    'suggested_action', 'reason_codes', 'is_declining_label', 'trend_direction',\n",
    "    'impressions_90d', 'clicks_90d', 'sessions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr',\n",
    "    'engagement_rate', 'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'word_count',\n",
    "]\n",
    "df['is_declining_label'] = df['trend_direction'].eq('down').astype(int)\n",
    "out = df[output_columns].copy()\n",
    "output_dir = Path('work/outputs')\n",
    "if not output_dir.exists() and Path('../../').exists():\n",
    "    output_dir = Path('../../work/outputs')\n",
    "output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "output_path = output_dir / 'baseline_action_score.csv'\n",
    "out.to_csv(output_path, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "def precision_at_k(frame, k=50):\n",
    "    return float(frame.head(min(k, len(frame)))['is_declining_label'].mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "base_rate = float(out['is_declining_label'].mean())\n",
    "print(f'Wrote {len(out):,} ranked rows to {output_path}')\n",
    "print(f'Base rate of declining pages: {base_rate:.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'Precision@10: {precision_at_k(out, 10):.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'Precision@50: {precision_at_k(out, 50):.3f}')\n",
    "print(out.head(3).to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Top-10 review\n",
    "\n",
    "The table below is a human-review aid. Confidence is about how clearly the observed signals support the suggested action—not confidence that the action will cause traffic growth. The final column records what could make the recommendation wrong."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "top10 = out.head(10).copy()\n",
    "def confidence_note(row):\n",
    "    if row['impressions_90d'] >= 3000 and row['reason_codes'] != 'general_review':\n",
    "        return 'medium-high: visible demand plus multiple review signals'\n",
    "    if row['impressions_90d'] >= 500 and row['reason_codes'] != 'general_review':\n",
    "        return 'medium: enough visibility, but inspect page context'\n",
    "    return 'low-medium: ranking is directional because demand is limited'\n",
    "\n",
    "def what_could_be_wrong(row):\n",
    "    if row['avg_position'] == 0:\n",
    "        return 'No position data; the position component should not be interpreted.'\n",
    "    if row['word_count'] == 0:\n",
    "        return 'Word count is missing or unmeasured; thin-content reasoning may be incomplete.'\n",
    "    return 'Correlation is not causation; topic, intent, competition, or client mix may explain the signal.'\n",
    "\n",
    "review = top10[['baseline_rank', 'content_id', 'suggested_action', 'reason_codes',\n",
    "                'baseline_action_score', 'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr',\n",
    "                'days_since_last_update', 'word_count']].copy()\n",
    "review['confidence_note'] = top10.apply(confidence_note, axis=1).to_numpy()\n",
    "review['what_could_be_wrong'] = top10.apply(what_could_be_wrong, axis=1).to_numpy()\n",
    "print(review.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Weak picks + leakage check\n",
    "\n",
    "A weak pick is not necessarily a coding failure: it is a page the rule ranks highly even though a human may not have enough evidence to act. I will inspect high-ranked rows with low visibility, no explicit reason code, missing measurements, or no valid position.\n",
    "\n",
    "Leakage check: the score and reason codes use only current observable content/performance fields. `trend_direction`, `trend_pct`, and `is_declining_label` are used only after ranking to measure the proxy outcome. No product flags, client IDs, or future-window columns are used as score inputs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "weak_mask = (\n",
    "    (out.head(50)['reason_codes'] == 'general_review')\n",
    "    | (out.head(50)['impressions_90d'] < 250)\n",
    "    | (out.head(50)['avg_position'] == 0)\n",
    ")\n",
    "weak_picks = out.head(50).loc[weak_mask, [\n",
    "    'baseline_rank', 'content_id', 'baseline_action_score', 'reason_codes',\n",
    "    'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr', 'word_count'\n",
    "]].head(10)\n",
    "print('Weak-pick candidates:')\n",
    "print(weak_picks.to_string(index=False) if len(weak_picks) else 'None found in the top 50.')\n",
    "\n",
    "score_input_columns = {\n",
    "    'impressions_90d', 'avg_position', 'ctr', 'days_since_last_update',\n",
    "    'word_count', 'engagement_rate', 'scroll_rate', 'sessions_90d'\n",
    "}\n",
    "forbidden_columns = {'trend_direction', 'trend_pct', 'is_declining_label', 'client_id', 'content_id'}\n",
    "print('Forbidden leakage fields excluded from score:', sorted(forbidden_columns))\n",
    "assert not (score_input_columns & forbidden_columns)\n",
    "assert 'baseline_action_score' in out.columns\n",
    "assert out['baseline_rank'].is_unique\n",
    "print('Leakage check: PASS — target/trend fields and identifiers are not score inputs.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Self-check\n",
    "\n",
    "- [x] The rule is explained in plain language before the code.\n",
    "- [x] The two signal checks are visible × freshness and visible search opportunity.\n",
    "- [x] Reason codes and suggested actions make the queue auditable.\n",
    "- [x] The ranked CSV is written to `work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv`.\n",
    "- [x] The top 10 includes an action, reason code, confidence note, and possible failure mode.\n",
    "- [x] Weak picks are explicitly inspected.\n",
    "- [x] Precision@10, Precision@50, and the base rate are reported.\n",
    "- [x] The score excludes `trend_direction`, `trend_pct`, `is_declining_label`, and identifiers.\n",
    "- [x] Claims remain observed, directional, and decision-support—not causal or guaranteed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "checks = {\n",
    "    'data_loaded': len(df) > 0,\n",
    "    'queue_written': output_path.exists(),\n",
    "    'top_10_reviewed': len(review) == min(10, len(out)),\n",
    "    'base_rate_reported': 0 <= base_rate <= 1,\n",
    "    'score_is_bounded': out['baseline_action_score'].between(0, 1).all(),\n",
    "    'ranks_are_unique': out['baseline_rank'].is_unique,\n",
    "    'leakage_check_passed': not (score_input_columns & forbidden_columns),\n",
    "}\n",
    "for name, passed in checks.items():\n",
    "    print(f'{name}: {passed}')\n",
    "assert all(checks.values())\n",
    "print('Self-check complete.')"
   ]
  }
 ],
